# Frontend design lane

This repo uses the **Cursor Agent Stack frontend module**: Impeccable (direction + enforcement) + ui-ux-pro-max (lookup) + curated design references + [design resource library](../design-refs/library.md).

Apply when editing UI, CSS, or layout — not for API/backend-only changes.

## Sequence (do not invert)

Root cause of generic UI: lookup (`ui-ux-pro-max`, Superdesign) ran before Impeccable committed a world.

1. Read root **`PRODUCT.md`** and **`DESIGN.md`**. If missing, **`/impeccable init`** (or `shape`) once — do not invent context.
2. **Named extreme** — write purpose, tone, constraints, and **one** direction before the first CSS rule. Not a blend. Default away from Inter / Roboto / Arial / Space Grotesk unless the brief wants restraint. Reference images beat vibe adjectives.
3. Then **ui-ux-pro-max** / one awesome-design-md brand / Superdesign — **against** that extreme.
4. Components: official shadcn MCP, then **react-bits** for personality motion, then hand-roll.
5. Motion: **Motion** (`motion/react`). **transitions-dev** for overlays / page transitions. **scroll-craft** for a scroll-driven story (copy the skill into `.cursor/skills/scroll-craft/` — Cursor does not load Claude's plugin marketplace).
6. **Verify** with a real 1× screenshot of the whole view vs before. Source review is not visual proof. Native `<select>` popups are invisible to tab screenshots — do not claim them verified.
7. Same element rejected **twice** → stop polishing execution; ask if the concept is wrong.
8. Open creative briefs: do not label the conservative option "(Recommended)."

Library (adopt / reject, including Relume / Spline / Studio): **`.cursor/design-refs/library.md`**.

## Command shortcuts

| Intent | Command |
|--------|---------|
| First-time setup | `/impeccable init` |
| UX review | `/impeccable critique <surface>` |
| A11y / quality | `/impeccable audit <path>` |
| Typography pass | `/impeccable typeset` |
| Pre-ship cleanup | `/impeccable polish <target>` |
| Browser variants | `/impeccable live` (dev server + CSP setup) |
| Amplify bland | `/impeccable bolder` |
| Tone down | `/impeccable quieter` |

## Hooks (automatic)

- **Project**: Impeccable design detector on UI edits (`.cursor/hooks.json`).
- **Global**: secret-guard + session checkpoint from `~/.cursor/hooks.json` — stacks cleanly; do not duplicate checkpoint hooks in the repo.

## Stack pairing

| Tool | Role |
|------|------|
| **Impeccable** | Authors `PRODUCT.md` / `DESIGN.md`. 23 commands, detectors. |
| **ui-ux-pro-max** | Palette/stack/UX lookup (Python CSV) — after step 2. |
| **design-refs/** | 3–5 brand links + `library.md` (not vendored YAML dumps) |
| **Superdesign** | Optional Marketplace plugin — critique / palette only. Never overwrite `DESIGN.md`. |

Preserve committed brand tokens in `DESIGN.md` unless `/impeccable typeset`, `/impeccable colorize`, or the user explicitly requests a redesign.

## Anti-patterns (confirm on the screenshot)

- Full-bleed hairline dividers on data-heavy sections, unless asked.
- Box-shadow / border too close to the background.
- Native OS form chrome in a custom-themed app.
- Skipping to ui-ux-pro-max on a new screen.
- Treating a placeholder mock as the real product UI.

## Hybrid (UI + WebGL)

If `.cursor/skills/r3f-three/` exists, use **3d-interactive-lane.mdc** for `scenes/` and R3F files — not this rule. Do not `/impeccable polish` WebGL. See docs/HYBRID.md in cursor-agent-stack.
